{"id":"20260825T230437.840224479Z-f0ff25e6","time":"2026-08-25T23:04:37.840224479Z","session_id":"session-20260825T224244.627431870Z","task_id":"task-1787697764627665115","source":"system","kind":"workflow.completed","summary":"candidate ready for governed admission","payload":{"audit":"schema: awareness.diff_audit/v1\ndecision: pass\navailability: available\ninput_trust: caller_supplied\ndigest: 46274833def5c0e08161eb0397b3c555354919a61e987ee54bb5adab00ce434c\nchanged_files_count: 3\nfindings_count: 0\n\nNo blocking findings found in supplied diff.","implementor":"claude","plan":"Implement Repo.CandidateDiff as the repository-backed intent-to-add strategy: register candidate paths with `git add --intent-to-add -- .`, then return the tracked and new-file patch verbatim from `git diff --no-ext-diff --binary`. This preserves normal .gitignore handling, reports an empty clean tree without error, and avoids staging file contents. Replace the workflow’s plain Diff call with CandidateDiff so the same complete patch reaches Sensei audit, reviewer input, and change reporting.","publication":"not_offered","review":"Sensei is authoritative/current and its critical invariant says: “The reviewer judges the whole candidate, including files the worker created.” CandidateDiff uses intent-to-add plus a verbatim binary diff, and Engine routes the same complete patch to audit, review, and reporting. The supplied bound-diff audit passed and validation passed.","workspace":"/tmp/proofbench/proof-v6/internal-gitx-a4fa351/COLD/.2-worktrees/task-1787697764627665115"}}